{
  "cell": "bias_core_startup",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py -- see layout/README.md",
    "for the recipe this follows (ported from 2AMLogic/sky130-trng) and",
    "issue #38 (part of #34, itself a follow-on from #30/#36/#37) for why",
    "this is a standalone proof cell rather than the full design/bias_core.sch",
    "composition.",
    "",
    "This is design/netlist/bias_core.spice's XKS0..XKS4 / XKA / XKAN / XKPD",
    "/ XKICK group -- design/bias_core.md's startup kick chain: a 5-stage",
    "diode-connected NFET stack (XKS0..XKS4, L=8 W=1 each, chained VDD ->",
    "KS1 -> KS2 -> KS3 -> KS4 -> NKG) plus a PFET (XKA) and two more NFETs",
    "(XKAN, XKPD) that mirror/pull down the kick node, and a final NFET",
    "(XKICK) that injects the kick pulse onto PG. 9 devices total, all",
    "sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 / sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 -- none of",
    "them are the sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40 device affected by",
    "2AMLogic/klayout-tools#1894, so (unlike bias_core_pnp8_leg/",
    "bias_core_xq1_xqr) this group is not expected to hit that gap.",
    "",
    "Each device is one klt gen mos_array call (rows=1 cols=1, dummy=0,",
    "gate_contact=true so every gate lands on a routable metal pad -- every",
    "gate here ties to a real net, not a bare pins[] label) -- nine",
    "1x1 blocks placed explicitly and wired by hand, following",
    "bias_core_settle_flag's own multi-block recipe (distinct devices with",
    "distinct per-terminal nets) rather than bias_core_pnp8_leg's single",
    "matched-array generator call (these nine devices do not match each",
    "other the way an 8:1 ratio leg's unit devices do).",
    "",
    "Floorplan: XKS0..XKS4 sit in one row (kpd, ks4, ks3, ks2, ks1, ks0 left",
    "to right), placed so each stage's U0_S (west-facing) meets the next",
    "stage's U0_D/U0_G (east-facing) directly across a small gap --",
    "mos_array's S is always drawn on the block's own west edge and D on",
    "its east edge, so the chain's VDD -> KS1 -> KS2 -> KS3 -> KS4 -> NKG",
    "direction runs right to left (XKS0 rightmost, XKS4 leftmost) for every",
    "adjacent pair to land on opposite-facing ports. XKICK and XKAN are",
    "mirrored (orientation: mirror_x, which negates local x and swaps",
    "U0_S/U0_D's east/west facing -- gen.md's own _ORIENTATION_DIRECTION_MAP",
    "-- note klt's own offset_um semantics: for a mirror_x block, origins_um",
    "places the block's PRE-mirror local x=0 corner, i.e. the block's",
    "resulting bbox_x1, not bbox_x0 -- the block extends further NEGATIVE",
    "x from there) so their own U0_S faces the chain/tap it needs to reach",
    "directly rather than needing a reach-around.",
    "",
    "KNOWN GAP hit building this recipe, reported generically per this",
    "repo's friction protocol: a two-stage 'stages'/blocks[].from_stage",
    "composition (layout/ro_stage/cell.json's own technique, used by",
    "bias_core_pnp8_leg's predecessor drafts) that re-places an EARLIER",
    "stage's flattened composed cell as one opaque block and then routes a",
    "bundle net onto several of that block's own promoted pins[] ports at a",
    "higher routing.layer_role reproducibly fails klt gen-compose's",
    "automatic via-drop with a same-layer li1.space.1-style spacing report",
    "against 'block core's own drawn geometry' for EVERY pairwise leg among",
    "the promoted ports -- even though the identical ports, routed directly",
    "(not through a from_stage promotion) in a single gen-compose pass with",
    "a per-net connectivity[].layer_role override (this cell's own 'nkm'",
    "net, below -- the same per-net-layer_role technique",
    "bias_core_settle_flag's README documents, klayout-tools#1655), land",
    "clean. This cell.json therefore uses the single-pass per-net",
    "layer_role technique instead of 'stages' -- see 'nkm' below -- and the",
    "from_stage failure is filed as",
    "2AMLogic/klayout-tools#1917 with a reduced repro (see that issue for",
    "the exact reproduction cell.json and response fields).",
    "",
    "XKA's PFET well is tied to VDD by NWELL-MERGING nwell_tap with XKA",
    "(placed so their bboxes overlap by ~0.10 um -- see",
    "bias_core_settle_flag/README.md's own '0.10 um nwell overlap' worked",
    "example and gf180-temp-por precedent: an NMOS body/substrate tie is a",
    "globally synthesized net regardless of any drawn contact (klt",
    "extract's sky130 deck: 'an NMOS body's terminal always falls back to",
    "the curated deck's synthesized substrate_net global'), confirmed",
    "empirically against this repo's own klt build (two mos_array nfets 100",
    "um apart, no shared geometry: both extract body='vsubs', the SAME",
    "net) -- so psub_tap only needs ONE routed strap into the real 'vss'",
    "bus anywhere, not one per NFET. A PFET's well is NOT globally",
    "synthesized this way (klt extract: 'unlike a PMOS body...'), so XKA's",
    "own well tie is real, physical nwell-merging, not routing alone."
  ],
